  "id": "stroop-colorword-interference-test",
  "term": "Stroop Color–Word Interference Test",
  "definition": "The Stroop Color–Word Interference Test is a neuropsychological assessment used as a cognitive outcome measure. In this source, it is treated as reflecting higher-order executive functioning, and poorer performance on it was one of the specific cognitive changes noted in some patients after deep brain stimulation.",
