      "reasons": [
        "The definition claims that the Stroop Color–Word Interference Test “reflect[s] higher-order executive functioning,” but the packet only states that mild, specific negative effects were observed on “higher-order executive functions” and separately reports a decline on the Stroop test; it does not explicitly link the Stroop Color–Word Interference Test to higher-order executive functioning in this source.",
        "The definition states that “poorer performance on it was one of the specific cognitive changes noted in some patients after deep brain stimulation.” The packet reports group-level meta-analytic findings (“patients undergoing DBS showed a more significant decline” on the Stroop test) and “within the assessed cognitive domains, mild, specific negative effects,” but does not support the phrasing “some patients after” as written."
      ],
